From 0e9e6145d6879f4388addff05ebaa0163f9e4796 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:04:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Trace rays with VK_KHR_ray_query; bind 7 descriptor sets

Android GPUs expose ray queries but not ray tracing pipelines, and bind at
most 8 descriptor sets (Turnip: 7); the path tracer needed 12.

- the 8 raygen shaders are compute shaders (8x8 groups, 3D for volumetrics);
  closest-hit, miss and alpha-test any-hit logic is inlined in RaygenCommon.h
- TLAS, global uniform, blue noise, cubemaps, render cubemap and portals are
  copied each frame into one combined set; the other sets are renumbered
- pipeline/shader stages RAY_TRACING -> COMPUTE; device needs ray query
  instead of ray tracing pipeline
- startup check of descriptor and compute limits

Pixel-identical to the ray tracing pipeline on lavapipe (Quake start map,
30 deterministic frames); a deliberately broken shader changes 97% of pixels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K7ddVeaJCm7c4L64HWexay
